1
00:08:53,333 --> 00:08:59,333
Searching for Amani is a documentary film directed by Debra Aroko.

2
00:17:46,666 --> 00:17:52,666
A 13-year-old aspiring journalist investigates his father’s mysterious murder
within the boundaries of one of Kenya’s largest wildlife conservancies.

3
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
As a ravaging drought encroaches, his quest to find the killer shifts as
the collateral damage of a warming world is revealed.

4
00:35:33,333 --> 00:35:39,333
Self, played by Simon Ali.

5
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:32,666
The Innsbruck Nature Film Festival (INFF) is an annual film competition
focusing on nature, environment, and sustainability.

6
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Based in Innsbruck, Austria, it was founded in 2002 by the
Tyrolean Environmental Ombudsman, Johannes Kostenzer.

7
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
In 2013, the festival transitioned from local nature film days
to an internationally oriented competition.

8
01:11:06,666 --> 01:11:12,666
In 2025, the festival attracted more than 13,000 visitors who participated in various event
formats, including film screenings, discussion panels, and supporting programs.
